@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/dispatcher#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .
@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .

<> a orexis:SelfGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO THIS AGENT IS: the dispatcher, and this document is its own by the self it states. Booted as
#  "dispatcher", the agent checks that this is so.
#
#  WHAT IT RUNS: it plans both vans' routes and walks them, in the packages' words, since the
#  courier's domain has none for an agent. Its world ships no rules, so it is no deliberator.

:dispatcher a orexis:Self , planning:Planner , execution:Executor .

#  WHAT ITS SEARCH MAY SPEND IN A PASS, a stance (knowledge/domain/kernel/stance.md): the two parcels
#  are one coupled want whose search costs 228 candidates (measure-the-search), past planning's 32 and
#  past 128 too. `tests/test_dispatcher.py` boots this world with no budget of its own and finds the
#  joint plan in one pass at this figure, and walks it.
:dispatcher planning:budget 256 .
